A||N||4||Monkeyman||Sway bar size||||5||
Z||000000||Monkeyman||08-09-2000||02:29 AM||||What size is the front (only) sway bar on an '85 GT?  Need to know so I can order saddle bushings.  Also, JC Whitney has different sized brackets for same.  Large and small.  Which one of those???<P>------------------<BR>Dave-<BR>Grape Ape ('85GT)||||reg||5
Z||000001||Oreif||08-09-2000||02:31 AM||||The front stock sway bar is 7/8" the aftermarket ones are 1". That might also be the difference in the brackets also.<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/LOGO3.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000002||Monkeyman||08-09-2000||02:37 AM||||So...I should get the smaller bracket??  I hate to move the wifes car and jack mine up to look under it and measure.  Good copy on the 7/8" bar, though.  I guess I'll order the smaller bracket and see if it works.  Thanx.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Taijiguy||08-09-2000||09:21 AM||||Use an open end wrench to determine the size. Slip the wrench over the bar like it were a bolt head. Whatever size wrench fits best is the diameter of the bar!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>(Lube up the bar and those new poly bushings with some of that stick lubricant made for car door hinges and latches, it's resistant to washing out, and will keep them quiet longer)<P>-Taiji||||reg||1
Z||000004||Monkeyman||08-09-2000||10:53 AM||||I'm pretty sure it's stock so I'll just go with 7/8".  What the heck.  The worst that happens is that I'm wrong and I have to ride around without a swaybar until I can get some other parts.  No biggie.||||reg||1
